+# S5-CLM-00003487 frontier
+
+The exact claim is:
+
+```text
+∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → Set.Infinite {p : ℕ | IsFirstKindChainOfLength p k}.
+```
+
+`IsFirstKindChainOfLength p k` requires a positive exact length, primality of
+every generated term at indices below `k`, and non-primality at index `k`.
+The source record is byte-bound to the Formal Conjectures revision
+`2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669` and is annotated `research open`.
+
+The target-local frontier has four typed branches: a uniform proof, a checked
+counterexample/refutation, bounded computational exploration, and exact Lean
+root closure. The bounded branch is evidence only. It cannot discharge either
+the infinitude or finiteness quantifier. No branch currently reaches a terminal
+`proved` or `refuted` outcome, so the TARGET remains unfinished by contract.
+
+The mapping, candidate-human, and candidate-machine cut sets are empty for the
+sealed structural DAG. The substantive resolution cut set remains explicit in
+`frontier.json`; this prevents a frontier record from being mistaken for a
+proof receipt.
