+# Human resolution
+
+## Exact polarity
+
+The frozen source proposition is a `Claim`, not a negated claim:
+
+```text
+∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → Set.Infinite {p : ℕ | IsFirstKindChainOfLength p k}.
+```
+
+The source file describes this as a conjecture and leaves its body
+unresolved. The target package preserves that status. It does not treat the
+source body, a docstring, a finite computation, or a literature citation as a
+proof term.
+
+## What was checked
+
+The exact recurrence is `q ↦ 2q + 1`. For a bounded local enumeration with
+`p ≤ 10000`, exact starts were observed for lengths 1 through 6; none were
+observed for lengths 7 and 8 in that bound. Those observations are compatible
+with the conjecture and also compatible with a finite exceptional set. They
+therefore establish neither `Claim` nor `Not Claim`.
+
+The first branch that could prove the claim would need a uniform construction
+or a theorem yielding infinitely many starts for every positive exact length.
+A refutation would need one positive `k` together with a proof that its set of
+starts is finite. Neither object was found or assumed in this run.
+
+## Resolution
+
+No complete human proof or refutation exists in the target-local evidence.
+The outcome is `open`, and the worker cannot advance RELEASE to `x`. A future
+attempt must append new evidence under this same TARGET identity and must bind
+the same statement fingerprint before any terminal outcome is considered.
